{"authored" [] "sources" [{"question" "q-77950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/problem" "value" "Given that ${i,j,k}$ is the standard basis of ${R}^{3}$ and that the images of $i,$ $j,$ and $k$ under the action of a linear transformation $T$ are $⟨6,2,0⟩,$ $⟨-3,5,6⟩,$ and $⟨-1,2,7⟩,$ respectively, what is the standard matrix of $T?$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060116/state.json" "file_sha256" "3377500f01fe1e57d901ee3e1ae1b8c7ffa6e13bff2fee3807ecc82b8263344e"} {"question" "q-77950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/worked-solution" "value" "Every linear transformation in ${R}^{3}$ can be represented as a $3\\times 3$ matrix. The standard matrix representation of the transformation has columns that are the images of the vectors $i,j,$ and $k$ under the action of the transformation.\n\nTherefore, the standard matrix for the linear transformation is \n\n$$\nT=[\\begin{aligned}6 & -3 & -1 \\\\ 2 & 5 & 2 \\\\ 0 & 6 & 7\\end{aligned}].\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060116/state.json" "file_sha256" "3377500f01fe1e57d901ee3e1ae1b8c7ffa6e13bff2fee3807ecc82b8263344e"} {"question" "q-77950" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/moderate "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "05a740a6c02b37abdaeebf43897898fc03edc0913dcb46481d4c5781746136db"} {"question" "q-77950" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060116/state.json" "file_sha256" "3377500f01fe1e57d901ee3e1ae1b8c7ffa6e13bff2fee3807ecc82b8263344e"} {"question" "q-77950" "field" "selection" "attribute"