tors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ are the first and second columns of $T,$ respectively. \n\nTherefore, we have the following:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T[\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T[\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\n**Method 2**\n\nWe can find the images of the vectors in the standard basis ${i,j}$ by computing the matrix products $T\\cdot i$ and $T\\cdot j:$\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}T(i) & =T\\cdot i=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}1 \\\\ 0\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}] \\\\ T(j) & =T\\cdot j=[\\begin{aligned}2 & 3 \\\\ 1 & -2\\end{aligned}][\\begin{aligned}0 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]=[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]\\end{aligned}\n$$" "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060116/state.json" "file_sha256" "3377500f01fe1e57d901ee3e1ae1b8c7ffa6e13bff2fee3807ecc82b8263344e"} {"question" "q-43836" "field" nil "attribute" "question/difficulty" "value" :question.difficulty/easy "category" "ma_capture" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060116/activity-metadata.json" "file_sha256" "05a740a6c02b37abdaeebf43897898fc03edc0913dcb46481d4c5781746136db"} {"question" "q-43836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/type" "value" :answer-field.type/radio "category" "ma_widget" "file" "/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/question-capture-workers/linear/14060116/state.json" "file_sha256" "3377500f01fe1e57d901ee3e1ae1b8c7ffa6e13bff2fee3807ecc82b8263344e"} {"question" "q-43836" "field" "selection" "attribute" "answer-field/choices" "value" [["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ -2\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin{aligned}3 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$"] ["text" "$[\\begin{aligned}2 \\\\ 1\\end{aligned}]$ and $[\\begin